    "aeo": {
      "headline": "Findable on company and category, not on the job to be done. \"Ashgrove\" and \"independent wineries\" will match a search. \"Inventory software\" is close. A buyer asking an answer engine for \"winery inventory management\" or \"cellar operations software\" has to infer the rest. The line is clear. It is not yet the phrase a cellar manager would type.",
      "about": "The About is a story, which is useful, and it names the buyer (independent wineries, cellar teams of three). It never says the product category in the language operators search: bonded inventory, case-goods, depletion, lot tracking, DTC vs wholesale counts. Clever origin. Thin for answer engines."
    },
    "featuredVsPerformed": "Featured is company news: an Operations Hour podcast clip, the Ashgrove 2.0 launch carousel, and the company page. What actually performed is operator writing. The top posts are a lost-order story, a cellar-wall photo, a mistakes carousel, and a blunt line about distributors and on-hand by SKU. The pin board is a press kit. The feed already knows the other thing works."
  },
